$$\\begin{cases} 7x - 4y = 11 \\\\ kx - 2y = 5 \\end{cases}$$', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{5}{2}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$3$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{7}{2}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$7$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'C', NULL, E'For a system to have no solution, the lines must be parallel: they must have the same slope but different $y$-intercepts. Rewriting the first equation: $y = \\frac{7}{4}x - \\frac{11}{4}$, so the slope of the first line is $\\frac{7}{4}$. Rewriting the second: $y = \\frac{k}{2}x - \\frac{5}{2}$, so the slope of the second line is $\\frac{k}{2}$. Setting slopes equal: $\\frac{7}{4} = \\frac{k}{2}$, which gives $k = \\frac{7}{2}$. Since $\\frac{11}{4} \\neq \\frac{5}{2}$, the $y$-intercepts differ, confirming no solution when $k = \\frac{7}{2}$.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"equation_setup_error"},"B":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"arithmetic_slip"},"C":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"concept_gap"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 105, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-27"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-27","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);










